            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0471" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.733/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-13T17:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1939—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. Your 631, July 11, 9 p.m. and 632, July 11, 10 p.m. Our action and procedure
                    in applying for an exequatur for Linnell was taken without consultation with any
                    other government. Our request for an exequatur for the principal officer at
                    Prague was solely for the purpose of providing for the continuance of consular
                    facilities in the Prague region. If you perceive no objection, you may orally
                    inform Weizsaecker that you had assumed that such was the case and that you have
                    been informed by your Government that your assumption was correct. You may add
                    that it would be a matter of deep regret to your Government if the German
                    authorities refused to permit our Consulate General to continue to function in
                    Prague.</p>
                <p>In the circumstances, we prefer that you not consult with your British and French
                    colleagues regarding this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
